WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Welcome. This class shows how to observe
an agent system

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.200
without turning telemetry into an
uncontrolled copy of user data.

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.800
You will connect causal spans, measure
useful outcomes, minimize sensitive

4
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.400
content, diagnose the first wrong
transition, and prepare decision-ready

5
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.000
human escalation.

6
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.077
Use traces, metrics, logs, and evaluations
together because each answers

7
00:00:33.077 --> 00:00:38.154
a different question. A trace reconstructs
one run and its

8
00:00:38.154 --> 00:00:43.231
parent-child operations. Metrics reveal
trends, distributions, and

9
00:00:43.231 --> 00:00:48.308
service-objective performance across many
runs. Logs record discrete operational

10
00:00:48.308 --> 00:00:53.385
events. Evaluations judge behavior against
cases and rubrics. None replaces

11
00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:58.462
the others. Begin with decisions the team
must make: detect

12
00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:03.538
a quality regression, locate a failed
boundary, control spend, prove

13
00:01:03.538 --> 00:01:08.615
an external postcondition, explain an
escalation, or decide whether automated

14
00:01:08.615 --> 00:01:13.692
recovery is safe. Collect a signal only
when it supports

15
00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:18.769
a named decision, control, or obligation.
Request volume alone does

16
00:01:18.769 --> 00:01:23.846
not reveal useful outcomes. A full
transcript alone does not

17
00:01:23.846 --> 00:01:28.923
reveal aggregate reliability and may
violate data promises. Purpose should

18
00:01:28.923 --> 00:01:34.000
determine collection, resolution, access,
retention, and deletion.

19
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.500
Preserve causal structure across the run.
Assign the workflow a

20
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:45.000
trace identifier. Give every agent step,
model call, retrieval, tool

21
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.500
call, approval, guardrail, handoff,
verifier, and recovery action a span

22
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:56.000
with its own identifier, parent linkage,
timing, status, and failure

23
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.500
class. Record stable references to
workflow, prompt, model, tool, policy,

24
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:07.000
content, adapter, and evaluation versions.
Add low-cardinality fields for aggregation

25
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.500
such as operation type and terminal state.
Keep detailed evidence

26
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:18.000
behind access-controlled references rather
than copying it into searchable labels.

27
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.500
Correlation and idempotency identifiers
should connect provider requests and

28
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:29.000
external effects without containing
credentials or personal data. A portable

29
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.500
span envelope lets different provider
frameworks feed one product-level trace

30
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.000
while preserving adapter-specific request
IDs and feature limitations.

31
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.077
Measure outcomes, not activity alone.
Track task success and independently

32
00:02:45.077 --> 00:02:50.154
verified completion beside policy
violations, unsafe attempts, user

33
00:02:50.154 --> 00:02:55.231
correction, escalation, abandonment, tool
and retrieval failures, retry rate, and

34
00:02:55.231 --> 00:03:00.308
unresolved outcomes. Measure latency as
distributions and stage-level spans, not

35
00:03:00.308 --> 00:03:05.385
one average. Relate token use and
estimated cost to verified

36
00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:10.462
successful tasks so optimization does not
reward cheap failures. Segment

37
00:03:10.462 --> 00:03:15.538
by workflow and policy version, model,
tool, journey, risk class,

38
00:03:15.538 --> 00:03:20.615
supported language, and other meaningful
populations. Avoid high-cardinality labels

39
00:03:20.615 --> 00:03:25.692
that expose sensitive content or make
metrics unusable. Alert on

40
00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:30.769
error-budget burn, critical policy events,
duplicate-effect attempts, unresolved

41
00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:35.846
reconciliation, missing trace segments,
and material quality changes. A healthy

42
00:03:35.846 --> 00:03:40.923
endpoint and growing request count can
coexist with user harm,

43
00:03:40.923 --> 00:03:46.000
excessive cost, or declining completion.

44
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.857
Assume model and tool content is
sensitive. Inputs, outputs, retrieval

45
00:03:50.857 --> 00:03:55.714
queries, documents, tool arguments,
results, and approval notes may contain

46
00:03:55.714 --> 00:04:00.571
personal data, credentials, customer
content, or protected business

47
00:04:00.571 --> 00:04:05.429
information. Default to metadata, bounded
classifications, hashes, and secure

48
00:04:05.429 --> 00:04:10.286
references. Capture raw content only for a
documented purpose, permitted

49
00:04:10.286 --> 00:04:15.143
population, and controlled duration.
Redact before export, isolate tenants,

50
00:04:15.143 --> 00:04:20.000
encrypt data, enforce role-based access,
audit viewing, sample by risk

51
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.857
and debugging need, and propagate
deletion. Define residency and regional

52
00:04:24.857 --> 00:04:29.714
transfer rules where required. Short
retention is a control, not

53
00:04:29.714 --> 00:04:34.571
an inconvenience. Never collect hidden
reasoning as an operational requirement.

54
00:04:34.571 --> 00:04:39.429
A concise decision summary, tool record,
evidence reference, and policy

55
00:04:39.429 --> 00:04:44.286
result support diagnosis without asking a
model to reveal private

56
00:04:44.286 --> 00:04:49.143
internal reasoning. Observability that
violates the product's data promises is

57
00:04:49.143 --> 00:04:54.000
itself an incident.

58
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.231
Diagnose from the visible failure backward
to the first wrong

59
00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:04.462
transition. Compare each span's actual
input, output, authority, postcondition,

60
00:05:04.462 --> 00:05:09.692
and state with its contract. Classify the
first divergence before

61
00:05:09.692 --> 00:05:14.923
changing a prompt: model, prompt,
retrieval, data, tool, policy,

62
00:05:14.923 --> 00:05:20.154
orchestration, or infrastructure. A wrong
final answer may begin with

63
00:05:20.154 --> 00:05:25.385
stale retrieval. A duplicate write may
begin with a lost

64
00:05:25.385 --> 00:05:30.615
idempotency key. Contain ongoing risk and
preserve redacted evidence. Escalate

65
00:05:30.615 --> 00:05:35.846
when a trace indicates unsafe action,
cross-tenant data, repeated unknown

66
00:05:35.846 --> 00:05:41.077
outcomes, policy conflict, or impact
beyond automated recovery. The human

67
00:05:41.077 --> 00:05:46.308
packet should contain a redacted timeline,
affected targets, versions, confirmed

68
00:05:46.308 --> 00:05:51.538
facts, containment status, evidence
references, remaining uncertainty, and the

69
00:05:51.538 --> 00:05:56.769
exact decision required. It should not
contain secrets, unnecessary customer

70
00:05:56.769 --> 00:06:02.000
content, unsupported blame, or hidden
reasoning.

71
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.333
A support agent claims a policy exception.
The final model

72
00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:12.667
span looks fluent and the tool span
succeeded. Walking backward

73
00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:18.000
reveals that retrieval selected an expired
policy because the content-version

74
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.333
filter was missing. The verifier checked
citation format but not

75
00:06:23.333 --> 00:06:28.667
effective date. Classify the first
divergence as retrieval or data

76
00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:34.000
freshness, not model style. Disable the
affected route, preserve the

77
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.333
content and workflow version references,
add a dated-policy regression case,

78
00:06:39.333 --> 00:06:44.667
and give the reviewer a redacted timeline.
Changing temperature would

79
00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:50.000
not repair the failed boundary.

80
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.500
Choose one raw telemetry field from an
agent workflow. State

81
00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:01.000
the operator decision it supports, then
replace it with the

82
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:06.500
least sensitive metadata, classification,
hash, or secure reference that still

83
00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:12.000
supports that decision.

84
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:48.000
Checkpoint. Should a human escalation
packet include full customer prompts

85
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:54.000
and hidden model reasoning by default so
the reviewer has

86
00:08:54.000 --> 00:09:00.000
every detail?

87
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.714
No. Give the reviewer a redacted timeline,
targets, versions, containment,

88
00:10:05.714 --> 00:10:11.429
evidence references, uncertainty, and
required decision. Include content only

89
00:10:11.429 --> 00:10:17.143
when policy, purpose, permission, access,
and retention justify it. Hidden

90
00:10:17.143 --> 00:10:22.857
reasoning is not required for operational
accountability. If you chose

91
00:10:22.857 --> 00:10:28.571
full capture for convenience, return to
data minimization. If you

92
00:10:28.571 --> 00:10:34.286
removed every detail, add enough governed
evidence to reproduce the

93
00:10:34.286 --> 00:10:40.000
state transition and decide containment or
recovery.

94
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:46.400
Open the trace review activity. Define
spans for agent, model,

95
00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:52.800
retrieval, tool, approval, handoff,
verification, and recovery. Add quality,

96
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:59.200
safety, reliability, latency, token, cost,
and escalation metrics. Write the

97
00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:05.600
telemetry policy, diagnose one failed
trace, and prepare the redacted

98
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:12.000
human-escalation packet.

99
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:17.500
When ready, begin the knowledge check. You
will choose linked

100
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:23.000
traces for causal review, relate cost to
successful outcomes, minimize

101
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:28.500
raw content, find the first wrong
transition, and build a

102
00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:34.000
safe escalation packet.

103
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:38.667
Collect signals for decisions, preserve
causal structure, measure outcomes,

104
00:14:38.667 --> 00:14:43.333
minimize sensitive data, find the first
wrong transition, and escalate

105
00:14:43.333 --> 00:14:48.000
